[al:新概念英语（三）]
[ar:MP3 同步字幕版（美音）]
[ti:In the Public Interest]
[by:更多学习内容，请到VeryCD.com搜索“露珠”]
[00:00.40]Lesson 53 | 第53课
[00:02.65]In the public interest | 为了公众的利益
[00:09.65]What could not be reported in the official files? | 官方档案中无法记录的是什么？
[00:15.80]The Scandinavian countries are much admired all over the world for their enlightened social policies. | 斯堪的纳维亚诸国因其开明的社会政策而受到全世界的推崇。
[00:23.38]Sweden has evolved an excellent system for protecting the individual citizen from high-handed or incompetent public officers. | 瑞典已逐渐形成了一套完善的制度，以保护个人公民免受专横跋扈或不称职的政府官员的欺压。
[00:33.22]The system has worked so well, that it has been adopted in other countries too. | 这套制度运转得非常好，其他国家也纷纷加以采用。
[00:40.21]The Swedes were the first to recognize that public officials like civil servants, | 瑞典人最先认识到，像公务员、
[00:46.23]police officers, health inspectors or tax-collectors can make mistakes or act over-zealously in the belief that they are serving the public. | 警察、卫生检查员或税务官这样的政府官员都可能犯错误，或者自以为在为公众服务而做得过分。
[00:56.76]As long ago as 1809, the Swedish Parliament introduced a scheme to safeguard the interest of the individual. | 早在1809年，瑞典议会就引入一项保障个人利益的制度。
[01:06.75]A parliamentary committee representing all political parties appoints a person who is suitably qualified to investigate private grievances against the State. | 一个代表各党派的议会委员会任命一位称职的人员专门调查针对国家的个人申诉。
[01:18.63]The official title of the person is 'Justiteombudsman', but the Swedes commonly refer to him as the 'J.O.' or 'Ombudsman'. | 这个人的官衔是“国会司法专员”，但瑞典人通常称他为“J.O.”或“司法专员”。
[01:29.51]The Ombudsman is not subject to political pressure. | 司法专员不受政治压力的影响。
[01:33.72]He investigates complaints large and small that come to him from all levels of society. | 他调查来自社会各阶层的或大或小的申诉。
[01:40.31]As complaints must be made in writing, the Ombudsman receives an average of 1, 200 letters a year. | 由于申诉必须以书面形式提交，司法专员每年平均收到1200封信。
[01:48.78]He has eight lawyer assistants to help him and he examines every single letter in detail. | 他有8名律师助手协助工作，每封信他都亲自仔细审阅。
[01:56.26]There is nothing secretive about the Ombudsman's work, for his correspondence is open to public inspection. | 司法专员的工作毫无秘密可言，因为他的信件接受公众的检查。
[02:04.50]If a citizen's complaint is justified the Ombudsman will act on his behalf. | 如果公民的申诉属实，司法专员将代表他采取行动。
[02:11.26]The action he takes varies according to the nature of the complaint. | 他采取的行动视申诉的性质而定。
[02:16.00]He may gently reprimand an official or even suggest to parliament that a law be altered. | 他可以温和地批评一位官员，甚至可以向议会建议修改某项法律。
[02:23.23]The following case is a typical example of the Ombudsman's work. | 下面这个案例是司法专员工作的一个典型例子。
[02:29.28]A foreigner living in a Swedish village wrote to the Ombudsman complaining that he had been ill-treated by the police, | 一个住在瑞典村庄的外国人写信给司法专员，抱怨说他受到了警察的虐待，
[02:37.37]simply because he was a foreigner. | 仅仅因为他是个外国人。
[02:40.42]The Ombudsman immediately wrote to the Chief of Police in the district asking him to send a record of the case. | 司法专员立即写信给该地区的警察局长，请他寄来该案的记录。
[02:49.38]There was nothing in the record to show that the foreigner's complaint was justified | 记录中没有任何东西表明这位外国人的申诉属实，
[02:55.32]and the Chief of Police strongly denied the accusation. | 警察局长也坚决否认这一指控。
[03:00.56]It was impossible for the Ombudsman to take action, | 司法专员无法采取行动，
[03:04.52]but when he received a similar complaint from another foreigner in the same village, | 但当他接到同一村庄另一个外国人的类似申诉时，
[03:10.20]he immediately sent one of his lawyers to investigate the matter. | 他立即派了他的一名律师去调查此事。
[03:15.03]The lawyer ascertained that a policeman had indeed dealt roughly with foreigners on several occasions. | 律师查明，一名警察确实曾多次粗暴地对待外国人。
[03:23.18]The fact that the policeman was prejudiced against foreigners could not be recorded in the official files. | 警察歧视外国人这一事实无法记录在官方档案中。
[03:30.55]It was only possible for the Ombudsman to find this out by sending one of his representatives to check the facts. | 司法专员只有派一名代表去核实事实，才有可能查明真相。
[03:40.24]The policeman in question was severely reprimanded | 涉事的警察受到了严厉的训斥，
[03:44.20]and was informed that if any further complaints were lodged against him, he would be prosecuted. | 并被告知，如果再有人对他提出申诉，他将被起诉。
[03:51.78]The Ombudsman's prompt action at once put an end to an unpleasant practice which might have gone unnoticed. | 司法专员的迅速行动立即制止了一种可能一直不被察觉的恶劣行径。
